  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given circles are $x^2+y^2-8 x-2 y+1=0$ and $x^2+y^2+6 x+8 y=0$ Their centres and radius are\n$$\nC_1(4,1), r_1=\\sqrt{16}=4\n$$\n\n$$\nC_2(-3,-4), r_2=\\sqrt{25}=5\n$$\nNow, $C_1 C_2=\\sqrt{49+25}=\\sqrt{74}$\n$$\nr_1-r_2=-1, r_1+r_2=9\n$$\nSince, $r_1-r_2 < C_1 C_2 < r_1+r_2$\n$\\therefore$ Number of common tangents $=2$",
    "image": null
  },
